    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="59">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 59</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="59" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="350" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa on ciningces<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_59.lnote.oe.9-2"/> hirede gefeohte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_59.lnote.oe.10-2"/>, þolige þæs lifes, butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_59.lnote.oe.1"/> se<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_59.lnote.oe.11-2"/> cingc him gearian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="59" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="350" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ðam þe on cynincges hirde feohteð. Gyf hwa on kynincges hirede gefeohte, ðolie ðæs liues, buton him se kynincg geárian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="59" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="350" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa on cynincges hirde feohte, þolige þæs lifes, buton him se cynincg gearian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="59" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="351" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis in familia (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_59.lnote.oe.9"/> est in curia) regis pugnet, uitę suę reus sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_59.lnote.oe.10"/>, nisi rex<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_59.lnote.oe.11"/> ei misereri<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_59.lnote.oe.12"/> uelit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="59" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="351" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis pugnam fecerit in (regali<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_59.lnote.oe.9-3"/>) aula regis, careat uita, nisi ei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_59.lnote.oe.10-3"/> rex parcere uoluerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_59.lnote.oe.11-3"/>.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_59.lnote.oe.star"/> . . .</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="59" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="351" ed="#liebermann"/>[59] Si quis in curia regis sedicionem mouerit, amittat uitam, nisi quid ei rex misericordie prestare uoluerit (dignatus fuerit).</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="59" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="204" ed="#robertson"/>Be ðam þe on cynincges hirde feohteð. Gyf hwa on kynincges hirede gefeohte, ðolie ðæs liues, buton him se kynincg geárian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="284" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gif hwa on ciningces hirede gefeohte, þolige þæs lifes butan se cingc him gearian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="350" ed="#liebermann"/>(Von dem, der am Königshofe ficht. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_59.lnote.de.1"/> einer am Königshofe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_59.lnote.de.2"/> ficht, verliere er das Leben, ausser wenn der König ihm Gnade gewähren will.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of him who fights at the king's court. B) If anyone fights at the king's court, let him lose his life, unless the king will grant him mercy.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_59.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="205" ed="#robertson"/>Concerning those who fight at the king's Court. If anyone fights at the king's Court<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_59.robnote.n.2"/>, he shall lose his life, unless the king is willing to pardon him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IICn_59.whinote.n.7"/><pb n="470" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone fight in the king’s court, he is to forfeit his life, unless the king wishes to spare him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="285" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If anyone fights within the king’s household, he shall lose his life unless the king is willing to show mercy to him.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="350"><ref target="clause:Af_7">Af 7</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 7</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="353"><label>rephrases</label> <ref target="clause:Af_7">Af 7</ref> <quote>Likewise, II 57, 59: rephrased Af 4 – 4:2, 7 respectively</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_7">Af 7</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 59: Af 7</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="470"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_7">Af 7</ref> <quote>cf. Alfred 7</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="367"><label>likely reference to</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_6">Ine 6</ref> <quote>Likely references include [...] ii Cnut §59 (Ine §6)</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares Af 7.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 351, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">B adds rubric Be ðam þe on cynincges hirde feohteð</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">rex mi. ei <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">rex mi. ei Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">patrare di. f. <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">patrare di. f. Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Hk ohne</hi> d. f.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Hk, without d. f.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i. in c. <hi rend="italic">nur T; fehlt übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i. in c. only T; lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">erit <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erit T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ei rex <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ei rex Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u. m. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u. m. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyninges <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyninges Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">feohte <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">feohte Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">him se cyning g. wille <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">him se cyning g. wille Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.oe.9-3" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a. regis <hi rend="italic">Cb;</hi> regali a. <hi rend="italic">HDi</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a. regis Cb; regali a. HDi</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.oe.10-3" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">rex ei <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">rex ei Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.oe.11-3" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uelit <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uelit Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt Af.</hi> 15—17; 38—39, 2 (<hi rend="italic">o. S.</hi> 59. 71)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">there follows Af. 15—17; 38—39, 2 (above pp. 59. 71)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dass Cn den Af, nicht Ine 6 , hier benutzt, folgt aus Afs Worten <hi rend="italic">him wille</hi> und aus der Benutzung von Af 4 und 3 vorher.—Mehrfach wird er durch Hn benutzt: 12, 3. 13, 7. 80, 1; 7.—<hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> blutig fechten 5b. d</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">That Cn uses Af here, not Ine 6, follows from Af's words <hi rend="italic">him wille</hi> and from the use of Af 4 and 3 just before.—It is used several times by Hn: 12, 3. 13, 7. 80, 1; 7.—<hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> blutig fechten 5b. d</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_59.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd</hi>. Königshof 2. 7</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid</hi>. Königshof 2. 7</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_59.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. In. 6; Af. 7; <hi rend="italic">Be Griðe</hi>, 15.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_59.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. <hi rend="italic">huse</hi>, Ine; <hi rend="italic">healle</hi>, Af.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_59.whinote.n.7" n="7" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">470</biblScope></bibl><label>59</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">cf. Alfred 7</seg></note>
